{
  "source": "Structured persona vocabulary for the Influencer Studio nav section - gender, age range, hair/eye colour and aesthetic style tags, each carrying the prose fragment build_persona.py folds into a single Subject description. Not transcribed from the course; this is app-original vocabulary in the same spirit as the other technique banks.",
  "version": 1,
  "note": "A persona is descriptive spec content, like wardrobe/setting/mood - it is NOT one of realism_lint.py's 8 gated photorealism layers, so nothing here needs a DETECT keyword. Every field is optional; compose_persona() always returns something usable (falling back to 'a person', the same default SpecEditor.PLACEHOLDER_SUBJECT already uses) rather than raising, since there is no invalid combination here the way an over-specified lighting/colour pick can be. Deliberately excluded: any attractiveness, face-shape or body-shape control - a face or build belongs in the free-text `details` field as prose, the same way SpecEditor's own Subject field already works everywhere else in this app.",

